From: John Drummond <john.drummond@ultra-sss.com>
Subject: [PATCH] OpenGL: regenerate symbol shaders, bind ProjectionUBO for symbols, project the custom fill

Patches 0014/0030 changed the shared symbol GLSL (shaders/symbol_*.vertex.glsl, projectTileWithElevation) and the
SymbolDrawableUBO for the Vulkan globe/terrain work, but the checked-in OpenGL shader headers (include/mln/shaders/gl,
generated by shaders/generate_shader_code.mjs) were never regenerated, and the OpenGL symbol shader infos did not map
the ProjectionUBO block the tweaker now fills. On OpenGL every symbol/text/icon render test drew nothing (497 render
tests, 13 unit tests failed on OpenGL). Also:
- the custom drawable layer's fill and line tweakers did not upload the ProjectionUBO the fill/line shaders project
  through (0004; Vulkan: CustomDrawableLayer.Line/Fill failed, OpenGL: Fill);
- StyleConversion.Projection still expected the pre-hand-off `globe` evaluation (globe, globe) at zoom 3.

Regenerated headers: prelude.hpp and symbol_{icon,sdf,text_and_icon}.hpp only (the generator also rewrites
shader_source.* and the manifest, which carry hand-added Sky/Atmosphere/Terrain entries - those are not regenerated).

diff --git a/include/mln/shaders/gl/prelude.hpp b/include/mln/shaders/gl/prelude.hpp
--- a/include/mln/shaders/gl/prelude.hpp
+++ b/include/mln/shaders/gl/prelude.hpp
@@ -98,6 +98,10 @@
 vec4 projectTile(vec2 pos) {
     return u_projection_matrix * vec4(pos, 0.0, 1.0);
 }
+
+vec4 projectTileWithElevation(vec2 pos, float elevation) {
+    return u_projection_matrix * vec4(pos, elevation, 1.0);
+}
 )";
     static constexpr const char* fragment = R"(#ifdef GL_ES
 precision mediump float;
